                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "94078533",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197987092452",
                            "num_reviews": 120,
                            "playtime_forever": 44,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 44,
                            "last_played": 1622322544
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First things first: the main, though certainly not only, reason I'm not recommending this game is that its been sitting at the same development state for over a year now and as far as I can tell is teetering on the edge of abandonware status.  The game is first-person horror with clear influences from Fallout and Bioshock, though without the atomic age satire of the former or the philosophical undertones of the latter. The game cold-opens with you in a 1960s-esque bomb shelter which turns out to be the entrance to the massive Colony 42 complex, the rest of which unfortunately we still have no idea about since the game ends at the end of the introductory chapter and as mentioned the long-promised chapters to follow remain conspicuous in their absence. \n\nThe gameplay is decent if a little clumsy at times, with an overemphasis on darkness making it hard at times to determine if an object is one with which you can interact or not. A few decent jump scares here and there do help to set the tone somewhere around one of the better Silent Hills, and the devs did do a good job setting atmosphere for what was supposed to follow. They did not, however, successfully debug what is present. Few of the achievements actually trigger where they are supposed to, and numerous small bugs and crashes crop up far too frequently for my tastes, even for a free introductory teaser. I get that 2020 was a hell year for everyone and for all I know the dev team collapsed due to Covid or something, but all the good will in the world won't make this game complete. Should they ever return to the project, I may well revise this recommendation.",
